-\raggedright \footnotesize \textbf{Notes:} Computational profiling, sequential operations, and latency decoupling across $N=350$ queries evaluated on \texttt{terra\_baselines\_eval\_raw.json}. Total operations per query account for all discrete algorithmic and model execution stages. Both Category C and Category D execute identical deterministic self-correction mechanics: queries clearing NLI entailment resolve on Attempt 1 (1 retrieval + 1 NLI verification + 1 generator call = 4 operations), whereas queries failing entailment trigger expanded retrieval before halting on Attempt 2 (2 retrievals + 2 NLI verifications + 0 generator calls = 5 operations). Category C includes 40 queries halted pre-retrieval by the geometric pre-filter (1 operation each) and 1 borderline query (\texttt{C069}, 2 operations), yielding an average of \TerraCatCTotalOpsPerQuery\ ops/query (\TerraBenchmarkTotalOpsFormatted\ total operations across the benchmark, averaging \TerraOverallTotalOpsPerQuery\ ops/query). Component latencies are decoupled from query ingestion: isolated retrieval duration reflects subtraction of double-counted routing latency (Category B isolated retrieval is 668.5 ms), matching total benchmark latency within 0.02 ms. Category D's higher mean NLI latency (\TerraCatDDecoupledNliMS\ ms vs. \TerraCatCDecoupledNliMS\ ms in Category C) is driven by prompt context scale (mean 268,682 raw / 15,969 clamped characters of dense precedent vs. 7,231 raw / 801 clamped characters of sparse out-of-domain text), requiring greater prefill compute on the 70B model under identical 2-attempt logic. Financial costs fold in Gemma 3 12B routing (\$0.15/1M tokens), local zero-cost deterministic retrieval (\$0.00), and LLaMA 3.3 70B NLI grading and generation (\$0.60/1M tokens).
+\raggedright \footnotesize \textbf{Notes:} Computational profiling and stage latencies across $N=350$ queries from the canonical v2 evaluation (\texttt{data/terra\_canonical\_v2\_eval.json}). Operations per query count each stage (routing, retrieval, NLI grading, generation) that recorded non-zero time. Generator calls count queries with non-zero generation time. Routing, NLI grading and generation are means of the logged timing fields. Retrieval is the logged retrieval time minus routing time for hard-route queries (whose retrieval timer includes routing) and the logged value otherwise. The stages sum to the end-to-end time for Category~A and the single-shot baselines; for Categories~B--D a remainder not attributed to any stage averages \TerraCatBRemainderMS, \TerraCatCRemainderMS\ and \TerraCatDRemainderMS\ ms. Category~A recorded retrieval and NLI-grader time on every query. Category~C recorded no generation; for 74 of 75 queries the context was empty and the recorded grading time was under 1~ms. Costs are modelled, not metered: token counts are estimated from character or word counts, Gemma 3 12B routing is priced at \$0.15/1M tokens and LLaMA 3.3 70B grading and generation at \$0.60/1M tokens, a grader call is priced for every Category~B--D query (twice for refused Category~C and~D queries) and none for Category~A, and retrieval is priced at \$0.00. Pricing one grader call only where the recorded grading time was at least 1~ms gives \$4.66 per 1,000 queries overall instead of \TerraDeployedCostPerThousand.
